 dict(n="B Q29", topic="Systems (Human/Plant)", type="Structured", marks=4, text="Kaixin drew a chart of the human body system (Arms, Small intestine and Lungs linked to Organ P by arrows W, X, Y and Z).\n(a) Which organ does Organ P represent? Identify the system that organ P is part of.\n(b) Which arrow(s), W, X, Y or Z, contain(s) the most amount of oxygen in the blood?\nNadia measured her heart rate during jogging and reading (bar graph).\n(c) Explain why Nadia's heart beats faster when she is jogging, as compared to when she is reading.", answer="(a) Heart; circulatory system  (b) Y  (c) The heart pumped blood faster to transport more oxygen and digested food to all parts of the body and remove more carbon dioxide and waste materials away from the body.", fig=[(18,170,240,715,400),(18,245,690,600,895)]),
 dict(n="B Q30", topic="Systems (Human/Plant)", type="Structured", marks=4, text="The diagram shows the human respiratory system and a leaf (with its tiny openings).\n(a) State one similarity in the functions of the lungs and the tiny openings.\n(b) Name all the main parts of the human respiratory system.\nSamuel coated three leaves with oil: J — lower surface only; K — no oil; L — both surfaces. On the 4th day, leaves L and J had withered and died.\n(c) Explain why leaves L and J had withered and died.", answer="(a) Both allow gases to enter and leave the parts.  (b) Nose, windpipe and lungs  (c) Oil covered the tiny openings on the leaf surfaces, so there was no gaseous exchange with the surroundings.", fig=(19,190,205,805,455)),
 dict(n="B Q31", topic="Cycles", type="Structured", marks=5, text="Qi Jun released 3 similar fruits with wing-like structures of different lengths (7 cm, 5 cm, 3 cm) from a height of 1 m. Average time taken to reach the ground: 7 cm — 29 s; 5 cm — 10 s; 3 cm — 3 s.\n(a)(i) State the relationship between the length of the wing-like structure and the time taken for the fruit to reach the ground.\n(a)(ii) Explain how the wing-like structure helps in the dispersal of the fruit.\n(b) Why did Qi Jun release all 3 fruits from the same height?\n(c) Qi Jun found the seedlings of fruits A and B in a forest (second diagram). Which seedling will grow less healthily? Explain your answer.", answer="(a)(i) As the length of the wing-like structure increases, the time taken for the fruit to reach the ground increases.  (a)(ii) The wings allow the fruit to float in the air longer, so it can be carried over a greater distance.  (b) To ensure that there is only one changed variable, which is the length of the wing.  (c) Fruit B. Its seedlings are close together, so they will compete with one another for water, sunlight, mineral salts and space.", fig=[(20,160,235,800,560),(21,170,280,760,585)]),
 dict(n="B Q32", topic="Cycles", type="Structured", marks=4, text="Study the flow chart: Animals → 'Does it have a 4-staged life cycle?' Yes → 'Does it lay eggs in water?' Yes → mosquito; No → B. If not 4-staged → 'Does the young resemble its adult?' Yes → C; No → 'Does it spend most of its life cycle in water?' Yes → D.\n(a) State one similarity and one difference between animals C and D.\n(b) State an example of animal B.\n(c) Mosquito larva and pupa are found just beneath the water surface. How does spraying a layer of oil onto the water surface kill them?", answer="(a) Similarity: both have a 3-stage life cycle. Difference: the young of C resembles its adult but the young of D does not resemble its adult.  (b) Butterfly / mealworm beetle / moth  (c) The oil blocks the breathing tube, so there is a lack of air/oxygen."),
 dict(n="B Q33", topic="Cycles", type="Structured", marks=3, text="Wei Ling placed set-up G (green bean seed in wet soil) and set-up H (green bean seed in dry soil) inside two identical cupboards and observed the seeds after 5 days.\n(a) What was the aim of Wei Ling's experiment?\n(b) State two variables which must be kept constant in this experiment.\n(c) Write the 3 stages of the life cycle of a bean plant in order. (In the original paper, pupils draw the cycle.)", answer="(a) To find out how water affects the germination of seeds.  (b) Any two: the temperature of the surroundings; the number/type of beans in each set-up; the type/amount of soil in each set-up.  (c) Seed → young plant (seedling) → adult (bean) plant", fig=(23,160,250,805,430)),
 dict(n="B Q34", topic="Systems (Human/Plant)", type="Structured", marks=2, text="The diagram shows a skeleton.\n(a) State the system that works with the skeletal system to enable us to move.\n(b) State another function of the skeletal system.", answer="(a) Muscular system  (b) To protect our (internal) organs / to give the body its shape"),
 dict(n="B Q35", topic="Systems (Human/Plant)", type="Structured", marks=3, text="Mrs Lim wanted to find out how the size of the bread affects the rate of digestion. She cut 3 similar pieces of bread E, F and G into different numbers of pieces, added the same amount of digestive juice to each and weighed them again after 5 hours (graph).\n(a) State the changed variable of the experiment.\n(b) Describe and explain how the size of the bread affects its rate of digestion.", answer="(a) The size / exposed surface area of the bread  (b) Cutting breaks the bread down into smaller pieces, so more surface area is exposed to the digestive juices and the bread is digested faster.", fig=(25,180,180,805,670)),
 dict(n="B Q36", topic="Matter", type="Structured", marks=3, text="Meat sellers display meat in a meat chiller. The temperature inside the chiller is 4 °C and outside is 30 °C. Water droplets form on the front glass display.\n(a)(ii) Explain how the water droplets are formed.\n(b) The door of the meat chiller was accidentally left open for 20 minutes. Fewer water droplets were observed on the glass display. Give a reason why this happened.\n(c) Which method, A (trays standing upright on a rack) or B (trays stacked), should the meat seller use to dry the trays faster? Explain your answer.", answer="(a)(ii) The temperature outside the chiller is higher than inside. The warmer water vapour in the surroundings lost heat to the cold surface of the glass display and condensed into water droplets on the outside of the chiller.  (b) The temperature difference between the inside and outside of the chiller decreased, so the rate of condensation decreased.  (c) Method A. Water drips off the trays and more surface area is exposed, so the trays dry faster.", fig=[(26,330,200,610,350),(27,255,250,705,455)], note="Part (a)(i) (draw the water droplets on the diagram) left out — drawing task."),
 dict(n="B Q37", topic="Matter", type="Structured", marks=3, text="Qi Ying gently put a lump of playdough into a beaker containing 200 cm³ of water until it was fully submerged. The water level rose to 250 cm³ (see diagram).\n(a) What is the volume of the playdough?\n(b) The same lump of playdough is rolled into a ball and put back into the same beaker with 200 cm³ of water. What will happen to the water level compared with before? Explain your answer.", answer="(a) 50 cm³  (b) The water level will remain at the same level. Only the shape of the playdough changed; it has a definite volume, so it occupies the same amount of space.", fig=(28,330,225,595,395), note="Part (c) (draw the new water level) left out — drawing task."),
